  },
  {
    "episode_id": 95941,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95941.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "You know, and I think a large part of this is of course we all know about issues with the media and with the notion that the media sometimes tends to put a negative spin on things or positive spin on things depending on what the story is. This kind of ties in nicely to, you know, one of the main reasons we're here today was just to talk drums. Obviously, you are a big proponent of commercial drone use. You are the ranking member of the aviation subcommittee. I know this is a movement or a cause that is very dear to you. I also know you probably are well aware that as with politics and presidential races, media coverage of drone use is not necessarily a positive thing. There's not a positive spin put on drone use. Gatwick, of course, is the be all tell all of what drones are. I think that for America, that was a huge story that went a long way in implanting this negative procession into people's minds. And there, of course, there have been others, the random drones out in the, I think it was Colorado, Arizona, New Mexico, that area. But of course, there's other negative drone stories. And the fact is, and you know this, given your position, the immense ability for good that drones are capable of accomplishing. What do you think we can do to help positively shape the narrative in order to encourage commercial drone use?",
