    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95941.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Well, one in regard to the media and sort of the transition you did from the partisan politics to the media. I think that the media does create these sort of sensational stories. They like the more provocative things. And so sometimes the media just doesn't view a good story about drones as being something that's really as provocative or sensational as many of the media outlets like. But the reality is, especially thinking about COVID, you and I are doing this remotely despite the fact that we're in the same city right now. We are. We're doing this largely because of COVID, right? And so drones actually bring the ability to allow for better distancing. Drones actually allow for improved safety. They don't force the interactions. They allow for an autonomous vehicle to be brought into areas that may be otherwise deemed unsafe. And I think that not just because of coronavirus, just because of the evolution of technology, because of the efficiency, because of the improvements, the safety that they provide. I think that there's so many opportunities for us to be able to tell those stories. And look, you and I have discussed this in the in the past grant, but everything from here we are in South Louisiana going due damage assessments after a hurricane or disaster sending in a drone to a scenario that otherwise might not be safe because of perhaps an armed suspect or someone who's threatening violence, a condition that a chemical plant, a leak of some type of chemical that from a vessel, I mean, just look, we can go on and on and on. The ability to lower costs of doing pipeline inspections, just how ubiquitous this platform is and the fact that you can just slap any sensor on it and allow it to improve safety and bring back data to us at a lower cost. The potential for the drone industry is just incredible. And in fact, one company that I was recently talking with indicated that just since coronavirus, they have seen a 1,000% increase in business because of coronavirus. And so this just goes to show you the incredible potential of this platform moving forward. And it's important to keep in mind the United States needs to be the leader on this technology as we have led many other technological revolutions in the past.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
