    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "No, I'm kidding. You know, granted, you're exactly right. And one of the things, DJI technology, it is a good technology. They're drones. They have some impressive drones. But this whole guilt by association thing, it is real. And let me say it again, you're seeing it in 5G. I think that The sensitivity of some of the drug platforms, including within our national security law enforcement apparatus, is an area where we need to be especially sensitive and be thoughtful about where we're deploying some of these technologies. We have seen some of the just incredibly aggressive or predatory tactics of China when it comes to using technology to gain access to information or other intellectual property. And I agree with you 100%. And I think as a result of, in terms of your Apple scenario, in terms of the fact that one company right now just has a majority of the drones that are out there, that does not mean that will continue. I think the guilt by association with China combined with the fact that we have US manufacturers that are bringing on technology that rivals or even best the technology of the Chinese manufacturers. I think that people, when they have a choice in the United States and most of the world, when they have a choice, they're going to go with a US manufacturer over a Chinese manufacturing.",
