    "turn_text": "Yeah. Well, let me say a couple of things. Number one, you did indicate that a number of our industries here in South Louisiana, those that are dominant on the Gulf Coast, are involved in drone testing and drone technologies. Sensors. And so there is incredible interest. There's utilization in some of these industries. You're exactly right that it's not the level that it could or should be. Number two, I got to give a shout out. Nickel State University has a partnership. They're working with the Home A Terrible in Airport and others on the testing and utilization of the technology. You and I also talked about a provision that right now is in the house past Coast Guard authorization legislation that sort of allows the Gulf of Mexico to be this test bed for wing and ground for Testing effectively drone technology and of course you're doing it above water as opposed to above land above populated areas which which does introduce a factor of safety or reduces some of the threat or risk So so we are working on on improving the utilization, the awareness, but I think ultimately what we need to do, and I'd love to work with you on this grant, is putting together a conference or symposium with some of the manufacturers of drones and of technology and with some of the potential utilization opportunities, some of the applications of the drones just to help improve awareness of of capabilities, awareness of what some of the sensors and other cameras and applications you can put on the platform. Just to help folks understand the improved safety, the improved, as we mentioned before, surveying pipelines, getting into wetlands and other sensitive areas that are so dominant here. in South Louisiana and preventing environmental impacts yet being able to get the data that you need. I think there's so many opportunities here that we can pursue, but I think it is kind of education and helping to expose some of these folks to the potential role that drones play in improving safety here in South Louisiana and across the Gulf Coast.",
